# KEUR-INT-001 — organisation-internal reference must not reach a public repo.
# @implements ADR-061 (this repo is public; internal trackers/domains are not)
#
# keur is a PUBLIC project maintained by someone who also does paid work on
# internal systems. The easy leak is an internal ticket/wiki id or a work domain
# pasted into a doc or a commit — harmless-looking, but it exposes an employer's
# internal taxonomy (Confluence space + page id, ClickUp/FreshService ticket
# ids) or a private hostname to the world, and it is exactly the kind of thing
# you only notice AFTER the repo is public.
#
# This BLOCKS (not warns): once it is in a public git history it cannot be
# unpublished. Catch it at the pre-commit gate, where the fix is a one-line edit
# before the commit exists, not a history rewrite after the fact.
#
# Detection = pattern over text. Each regex is a concrete internal-reference
# shape seen in this repo's own near-miss (the ADR-061 grounding line that named
# a real Confluence page + ClickUp task). Generalise the shape, not the literal:
#   - Confluence space/page coordinate: SPACEKEY/<8+ digit page id>
#   - ClickUp task id: the 9-char base-36 task slug after the tool name
#   - internal tracker/wiki/domain names tied to the employer
# A legitimate mention of the *tool* ("we use Confluence") is fine — the rule
# fires on an ID or a work-domain, not the bare product name.
id: KEUR-INT-001
ilities: [confidentiality]
maturity: 2
title: Organisation-internal reference (ticket / wiki id / work domain) in a public repo
category: pii
severity: critical
engine: pattern
action: block
skip_comments: false
target:
  extensions: .md .txt .cpp .c .h .hpp .py .ts .tsx .js .jsx .go .java .rb .sh .yml .yaml .json .toml
  # The rules corpus holds detection patterns (not real data); eval/ holds
  # generated run data. Exclude both so the guard does not flag its own examples.
  exclude_paths: rules/ eval/ vendor/ node_modules/ .git/ build/ dist/ tests/fixtures/
patterns:
  - regex: \b(Confluence|CONF)\s+[A-Z]{2,10}/\d{8,}
    message: "Confluence space+page id (e.g. 'Confluence PLAT/21744320552') — an internal wiki coordinate. Replace with a generic phrase ('an internal RFC') or a public link. Suppress with keur:ignore KEUR-INT-001 only if this is intentionally public."
  - regex: \b(ClickUp|FreshService|Jira)\s+[0-9a-z]{7,10}\b
    message: "Internal tracker ticket id (ClickUp/FreshService/Jira). A public repo must not expose an employer's ticket taxonomy — refer to the work generically or link a public issue instead."
  - regex: (?i)@(theapsgroup|aps-group)\.(com|net|io)\b
    message: "Internal/work email domain in tracked content. Use a personal/public contact for a public project; keep the work identity out of the repo body."
confidence: 0.9
fix: "Remove the internal reference: replace an internal ticket/wiki id with a generic phrase or a public link, use a personal contact instead of a work email. If a mention is deliberately public and safe, add keur:ignore KEUR-INT-001 on that line with a reason."
